part mtg_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "MTG-1 · Payment holidays. A borrower with a dukat mortgage for their own home agreed before 2022-07-01 may suspend up to 8 instalments: 2 in 2022 Q3, 2 in Q4, 1 in each quarter of 2023; one loan per borrower (.1); asked for by notice, for an instalment due after the notice (.2); for a suspended month nothing is paid and no interest is charged, every later instalment moves one month, the term grows a month per suspension (.3)."
  note "No figure: the caps are literals the literal rule allows (L §7.1); the household's loan defs apply .3."

source mtg_1 "Mortgage Credit Act, MTG-1 Payment holidays (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version mtg1_v1
  cite mtg_1
  governs 2022-08-01..2023-12-31
  known 2022-07-14
  enters 2022-07-29
  note "MTG-1 v1, in force 2022-07-29 – 2023-12-31, published 2022-07-14; governs instalments falling due 2022-08-01 – 2023-12-31."
